## CI runs 39017316556 (ae182d9) and 39017672731 (0a26c88): job test FAILED in the first pytest step — 1 failed, 1129 passed, 4 skipped, 4 deselected:
===== 1 failed, 1129 passed, 4 skipped, 4 deselected in 112.41s (0:01:52) ======
E   AssertionError: assert ('<unmatched>' == '/{full_path}'
FAILED tests/test_r159_telemetry.py::test_consecutive_requests_never_share_or_inherit_a_trace - AssertionError: assert ('<unmatched>' == '/{full_path}'
tests/test_r158_test_baseline.py::test_pytest_summary_parser[===== 3 failed, 1053 passed, 4 skipped, 4 deselected in 149.15s (0:02:29) ======-expected1] PASSED [ 56%]
## also: governance 39017316555 on ae182d9 failed: pr=#PRNUM placeholder rejected by the status check (as designed); fixed in 0a26c88 (governance 39017672753 success).
## cause: server.py registers the SPA catch-all '/{full_path:path}' only if web/dist exists (server.py:1040). The local working copy has a built web/dist (untracked, from earlier builds); CI's test job does not build web/. The test hard-coded the local state. Test-design defect; the runtime records '<unmatched>' correctly when no route matches.
## fix (git diff):
diff --git a/tests/test_r159_telemetry.py b/tests/test_r159_telemetry.py
index e1bc594..7c5f533 100644
--- a/tests/test_r159_telemetry.py
+++ b/tests/test_r159_telemetry.py
@@ -468,8 +468,12 @@ def test_consecutive_requests_never_share_or_inherit_a_trace(auth):
     http = [x for x in _records() if x["kind"] == "http"]
     assert len(http) == 3 and len({x["trace_id"] for x in http}) == 3
     assert all(x["parent_span_id"] is None for x in http)
-    # the SPA catch-all answers unknown paths: the label is its template, never the raw path
-    assert http[1]["route"] == "/{full_path}" and "nonexistent" not in json.dumps(http[1])
+    # the SPA catch-all `/{full_path:path}` exists only when web/dist is built
+    # (log 106): then the label is its template, otherwise "<unmatched>" —
+    # never the raw path either way.
+    catch_all = any(getattr(rt, "path", "") == "/{full_path:path}" for rt in server.app.routes)
+    assert http[1]["route"] == ("/{full_path}" if catch_all else "<unmatched>")
+    assert "nonexistent" not in json.dumps(http[1])
     for h in http:                                   # every span of a trace hangs under its own http root
         for x in _records(h["trace_id"]):
             assert x is h or x["parent_span_id"] is not None
